# Git stores text blobs with LF, but a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true
# writes CRLF into the working tree. The evidence contracts fingerprint files by
# SHA256 over their on-disk bytes, so without this the params.yaml fingerprint --
# and any future fingerprint over a tracked text file -- depends on which
# platform performed the checkout rather than on the file's contents.
#
# Pinning the working tree to LF everywhere makes those hashes reproducible
# across platforms. It complements lineterminator="\n" on the pipeline's CSV
# writers: that covers files the pipeline writes, this covers files git writes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated binaries: never normalise, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.joblib binary
*.pq binary
*.db binary
